{# "Here is what happened to your bug." Sent ONCE, on Resolved or Declined.

   The one mail that decides whether somebody reports a second bug. It always
   carries the curator's reason, and the desk refuses to reach either status
   without one, because "we are not fixing this" with no explanation is the
   message that makes a person stop bothering.

   Not sent for Planned, In progress or Needs testing: being told a report moved
   between two internal states is noise, and noise is what teaches people to
   ignore the next mail. #}
{% extends 'emails/_base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'support.email.bug_outcome_subject'|trans({'%reference%': reference}, null, locale) }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a6a3f">{{ reference }} · {{ status_label }}</p>
  <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:19px;font-weight:600">{{ report.title }}</p>

  {% if report.outcomeNote %}
    <div style="padding:12px 16px;background:#f5eee0;border-left:3px solid #3f6152;border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap">{{ report.outcomeNote }}</div>
  {% endif %}

  <p style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6">{{ 'support.email.bug_outcome_thanks'|trans([], null, locale) }}</p>

  <p style="margin:22px 0 0">
    <a href="{{ site_url }}/known-issues" style="display:inline-block;background:#14160e;color:#fdfaf1;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px">{{ 'support.known.title'|trans([], null, locale) }}</a>
  </p>
{% endblock %}
